{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count of all assignments 0/1 satisfying CNF. n=12 variables. Clauses list: \n1: [-10,3] meaning ¬x10 ∨ x3\n2: [7,1] meaning x7 ∨ x1\n3: [-1,4] meaning ¬x1 ∨ x4\n4: [6,12] meaning x6 ∨ x12\n5: [-6,2] meaning ¬x6 ∨ x2\n6: [-8,5] meaning ¬x8 ∨ x5\n7: [-9,3] meaning ¬x9 ∨ x3\n8: [8,11] meaning x8 ∨ x11\n9: [10,9] meaning x10 ∨ x9\n10: [-11,5] meaning ¬x11 ∨ x5\n11: [-7,4] meaning ¬x7 ∨ x4\n12: [-12,2] meaning ¬x12 ∨ x2\n\nWe need count of satisfying assignments. We can analyze constraints.\n\nLet's denote variables: x1..x12.\n\nWe have pairs of clauses linking variables.\n\nLet's analyze systematically.\n\nClause 2: x7 ∨ x1. So at least one of x7, x1 is true.\n\nClause 3: ¬x1 ∨ x4. Equivalent: x1 → x4. So if x1 true then x4 true. If x1 false, clause satisfied regardless of x4.\n\nClause 11: ¬x7 ∨ x4. Equivalent: x7 → x4. So if x7 true then x4 true.\n\nThus if either x1 or x7 true, x4 must be true. So x4 must be true unless both x1 and x7 false. But clause 2 requires at least one true, so at least one of x1,x7 true. Therefore x4 must be true in all satisfying assignments. Good.\n\nNow clause 4: x6 ∨ x12. So at least one of x6,x12 true.\n\nClause 5: ¬x6 ∨ x2. Equivalent: x6 → x2. So if x6 true then x2 true.\n\nClause 12: ¬x12 ∨ x2. Equivalent: x12 → x2. So if x12 true then x2 true.\n\nThus if either x6 or x12 true, x2 must be true. Since at least one of x6,x12 true, x2 must be true in all assignments. So x2 true.\n\nNow clause 6: ¬x8 ∨ x5. Equivalent: x8 → x5.\n\nClause 8: x8 ∨ x11. So at least one of x8,x11 true.\n\nClause 10: ¬x11 ∨ x5. Equivalent: x11 → x5.\n\nThus if either x8 or x11 true, x5 must be true. Since at least one of x8,x11 true, x5 must be true. So x5 true.\n\nNow clause 1: ¬x10 ∨ x3. Equivalent: x10 → x3.\n\nClause 7: ¬x9 ∨ x3. Equivalent: x9 → x3.\n\nClause 9: x10 ∨ x9. So at least one of x10,x9 true.\n\nThus at least one of x10,x9 true, and if either true, x3 must be true. So x3 must be true. So x3 true.\n\nThus we have forced assignments: x2=true, x3=true, x4=true, x5"}}],"created":1790940945,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":3797,"total_tokens":4565,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-QxUWdxK5BvYinurTairwDgdF9KNXIf5T","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":3797,"prompt_ms":470.227,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12384171714511456,"prompt_per_second":8074.823436340322,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2409.397,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.1413259452411992,"predicted_per_second":318.3369116837118}}